  "title": "PPO \u00b7 full-finetune verl recipe (collapsed)",
  "group": "ablation",
  "analysis": "Full-parameter port of verl's PPO recipe to Qwen3-4B-Base and the DAPO math data: GAE single rollout, no KL loss, actor lr 1e-6, critic lr 1e-5, batch 1024/mini 256, clip 0.2, epochs 15, prompt 1024, response 8192. Stopped after 7 updates: mean response length rose from 1.6k to 7.5k tokens, training correctness fell from 0.101 to 0.048, and policy entropy fell from 0.92 to 0.18. Together with the earlier LoRA run the same collapse appears across LoRA versus full fine-tuning, KL on versus off, actor lr 3e-5 versus 1e-6, one versus five samples per prompt, and batch 256 versus 1024, while our GRPO runs (eight-sample group-mean baseline) are stable at the same 8192 response budget. This isolates the learned critic/GAE advantage estimator: on this hard long-horizon task it yields a length-biased advantage where the group baseline does not. Unverified hypothesis for later: SkyRL's PPO implementation may be faulty, since the same recipe trains in verl's own framework. PPO is set aside for now.",
